UART Controller

1. One Tx
2. One Rx

3. Assume common clock frequency
    a. Common baud rates: 9600, 115200, 4800, 19200, 38400, 57600
4. Assume common frame structure
    a. 7-9 data bits
    b. Single optional parity bit at the end (odd/even parity 1's)
    c. Idle on 1
    d. Drop to 0 indicates Rx
5. UART reads from its data reg (8 bits most common) and sends it over
    a. Any data packetization form 32 down to 8 is done externally from the UART by something like firmware or a DMA
    b. Single packets sent at a time
6. Assumed only Tx or Rx one at a time

